Appendix F — De-legalisation Risk Score Protocol

F.1 Components

Component Coding Weight
Legal basis Statute = 1; regulation = 2; executive guidance = 3; voluntary arrangement = 4 0.5
Political-cycle survival Survived one full alternation of executive power = 0; not yet tested = 1; reversed = 2 0.3
Active repeal agenda No = 0; unknown = 1; yes = 2 0.2

The weighted score ranges from 0.5 to 4.0. A score above 2.5 indicates high de-legalisation risk. The weights are pre-registered and must not be adjusted after data collection begins. The score is published alongside the instrument count; a jurisdiction with many instruments but a high score is not durable.

F.2 Worked example: EO 14292 and the 2024 Framework

The 2024 Framework for Nucleic Acid Synthesis Screening rested on executive action rather than statute (legal basis = 3). It was paused by a subsequent executive order before surviving a full political cycle (political-cycle survival = 2). A replacement was directed but not issued, and the policy remained paused (active repeal agenda = 2). Weighted score: (0.5 × 3) + (0.3 × 2) + (0.2 × 2) = 1.5 + 0.6 + 0.4 = 2.5. The case is at the threshold of high risk, and the framework predicts that statutory instruments in comparable jurisdictions will survive equivalent political shocks more often .

