Appendix H — Indicator Definitions and Validity Notes

H.1 Dashboard indicators (five to eight)

1. Screening red-team pass rate. Percentage of tested provider screening systems that detect a standardised panel of fragmented and AI-redesigned sequences of concern. Denominator: providers tested, not providers listed. Date and evaluator stated.
2. Patch latency and deployment coverage. Days between disclosed evasion and deployed patch; percentage of known providers with the patch installed. The Paraphrase case is the anchor: ~10 months latency, ~3% residual evasion .
3. Registry coverage versus independent identification. Percentage of clinical trials or research projects that appear in a public registry relative to those independently identified through literature or press. A low ratio indicates a registration gap, not necessarily a governance failure, and must be interpreted with that confounder stated.
4. Price and availability by income group. Net price relative to GDP per capita; treatment-centre density; financing coverage. The CMS and NexCAR19 cases illustrate why list price alone is misleading .
5. De-legalisation risk score. Composite in Appendix F. Published alongside instrument count.
6. Deliberative inclusiveness. Count of legitimacy sub-criteria met (0–4), from Appendix A.5.
7. Implementation instability. Count of internally inconsistent primary-source reports on a programme’s own participation or performance. The CMS 32/33 case is the anchor .

H.2 Validity cautions

The GHSI record is the controlling caution: a preparedness index built for accountability did not predict COVID-19 mortality (GHSI r = 0.31) . The dashboard is therefore published as a profile, not a composite, until construct-validity testing is complete. Each indicator must be reproducible by an independent analyst from public sources; an indicator that cannot be reproduced is withdrawn and the withdrawal is published in the annual indicator-failure report. This rule is the operational meaning of the thesis’s “dashboard-before-index” commitment.

